# XSH poll() and ppoll()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# poll() is ppoll() with a null signal mask and a millisecond timeout, so
# a test about both runs its check through both (a failure names the
# function). Readiness is arranged with pipes, FIFOs, socket pairs and a
# regular file; whether a pipe is two-way is unspecified (pipe() page), so
# only the end meant for the operation is polled. The page does not
# constrain priority-band events, so POLLRDBAND, POLLWRBAND, POLLPRI and
# POLLRDNORM on pipes are not required. The values of revents bits other
# than those requested are required to be clear except for POLLHUP,
# POLLERR and POLLNVAL, which are conditions the call reports anyway.
# Lower bounds on waiting use CLOCK_MONOTONIC and allow for the clock's
# resolution; no upper bound is asserted (a guard alarm gives UNRESOLVED).
# Signals for the EINTR tests come from a child that repeats them or are
# made pending while masked. Not tested: terminals, priority bands,
# thread cancellation, an invalid ppoll timeout (the page does not say
# which are invalid, see the report).

assertion  XSH.poll.001
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       A pipe's read end holding data, polled for POLLIN, gives 1 from
           poll() and ppoll() with POLLIN set in revents, and the fd and
           events members are as they were.
test       t/001-pollin-pipe.c

assertion  XSH.poll.002
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       The write end of a pipe with room, polled for POLLOUT, gives 1
           with POLLOUT set in revents.
test       t/002-pollout-pipe.c

assertion  XSH.poll.003
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       POLLWRNORM is equivalent to POLLOUT: the write end of a pipe with
           room, polled for POLLWRNORM, gives 1 with POLLWRNORM set in
           revents.
test       t/003-pollwrnorm.c

assertion  XSH.poll.004
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Only the requested conditions are reported: a socket with data
           waiting that is also writable, polled for POLLIN alone, gives
           revents equal to POLLIN (ignoring POLLHUP, POLLERR and POLLNVAL,
           none of which applies), and an entry with events 0 on the same
           kind of socket gets revents 0 and is not counted.
test       t/004-only-requested.c

assertion  XSH.poll.005
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       With three entries (ready, not ready, ready) the return value is
           2, the not-ready entry's revents is 0 although it held another
           value before the call, and the two ready entries' revents are
           non-zero.
test       t/005-count.c

assertion  XSH.poll.006
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       An entry whose fd is negative has its events ignored and its
           revents set to 0 (although it held another value), and is not
           counted: with a ready pipe in a second entry the return value
           is 1.
test       t/006-negative-fd.c

assertion  XSH.poll.007
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       An fd that is not open, polled for POLLIN, gives POLLNVAL in
           revents and is counted: the return value is 1.
test       t/007-pollnval.c

assertion  XSH.poll.008
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       POLLNVAL is reported although it was not requested: an fd that is
           not open with events 0 gives POLLNVAL in revents and 1 from the
           call.
test       t/008-pollnval-unrequested.c

assertion  XSH.poll.009
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       The read end of a pipe whose last write end was closed, polled
           for POLLIN, has POLLHUP set in revents.
test       t/009-pollhup-pipe.c

assertion  XSH.poll.010
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       POLLHUP is reported although it was not requested: the same pipe
           read end with events 0 gives POLLHUP in revents and 1 from the
           call.
test       t/010-pollhup-unrequested.c

assertion  XSH.poll.011
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       POLLHUP and POLLOUT are mutually exclusive: the read end of a
           pipe whose last write end was closed, polled for POLLIN and
           POLLOUT, never has both in revents.
test       t/011-hup-excludes-out.c

assertion  XSH.poll.012
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#RATIONALE
class      required
since      2001
says       The hangup state of a FIFO persists: after a writer wrote a byte
           and closed, POLLHUP is set for the read end, and still set after
           the byte has been read, and in a later call.
test       t/012-fifo-hup-persists.c

assertion  XSH.poll.013
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       The hangup state of a FIFO lasts only until a process opens the
           FIFO for writing: after the persisted hangup, a new writer's
           open makes POLLHUP clear in revents while the writer stays open.
test       t/013-fifo-hup-cleared.c

assertion  XSH.poll.014
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#RATIONALE
class      required
since      2001
says       A FIFO that has been opened for reading but never had a writer is
           not in the hangup state: polling its read end for POLLIN (with a
           short timeout) leaves POLLHUP clear in revents.
note       Whether POLLIN is set for such a FIFO (a read would return
           end-of-file without blocking) is not asserted.
test       t/014-fifo-no-hup-without-writer.c

assertion  XSH.poll.015
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A regular file always polls true for reading and writing: with
           events POLLIN|POLLOUT the call returns 1 and revents holds both.
test       t/015-regular-file.c

assertion  XSH.poll.016
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       When the timeout (50 ms) expires with nothing ready (an empty
           pipe's read end), poll() and ppoll() return 0 and revents is 0.
test       t/016-expiry.c

assertion  XSH.poll.017
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With nothing ready and no signal, poll() and ppoll() with a
           250 ms timeout do not return before that interval has elapsed
           (measured allowing for the clock's resolution) and return 0.
note       Only a lower bound is asserted; the interval may be rounded up.
test       t/017-expiry-waits.c

assertion  XSH.poll.018
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With a zero timeout the call is a poll and does not wait: an empty
           pipe's read end gives 0 and a pipe with data gives 1 with POLLIN
           (a call that does not come back within the guard is UNRESOLVED).
test       t/018-zero-timeout.c

assertion  XSH.poll.019
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A timeout of -1 for poll(), and a null timeout for ppoll(), wait
           until a descriptor is ready: with an empty pipe that a child fills
           after a pause, the call returns 1 with POLLIN, and a byte can
           then be read (a call that does not come back within the guard is
           UNRESOLVED).
timeout    70
test       t/019-infinite-wait.c

assertion  XSH.poll.020
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A positive timeout is a maximum: with a 10 s timeout and a child
           that fills an empty pipe after a pause, poll() and ppoll() return
           1 with POLLIN (not 0) once the byte is there.
timeout    70
test       t/020-timeout-is-maximum.c

assertion  XSH.poll.021
anchor     functions/poll.html#ERRORS/EINTR
class      required
since      2001
says       A signal caught (handler installed without SA_RESTART) while
           poll() or ppoll() (null mask) waits on an empty pipe with a long
           timeout makes it return -1 with EINTR.
note       The signal comes from a child that repeats it every 20 ms.
test       t/021-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.poll.022
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/poll.html#ERRORS/EINTR
class      required
since      2024
says       With SIGUSR1 blocked and pending, ppoll() given an empty sigmask
           and nothing ready runs the handler (installed without
           SA_RESTART) and returns -1 with EINTR instead of waiting out a
           long timeout; the caller's mask is back (SIGUSR1 blocked) on
           return.
note       Q-87: nothing is ready here, so the unspecified case does not arise.
test       t/022-ppoll-unmask-eintr.c

assertion  XSH.poll.023
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A signal that the sigmask given to ppoll() blocks does not cut the
           wait short: with SIGUSR1 sent every 10 ms by a child during a
           300 ms call with nothing ready, the call does not return before
           the interval has elapsed (allowing for the clock's resolution).
note       The signal may become deliverable once the original mask is
           restored, so the result (0, or -1 with EINTR) is not asserted.
test       t/023-sigmask-blocks.c

assertion  XSH.poll.024
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       After ppoll() returns, the caller's mask is back: with SIGUSR2
           blocked by the caller (on top of whatever mask the test started
           with) and a sigmask holding all signals, the mask afterwards is
           the same one (checked for a set of common signals), after a
           timeout return and after a return with a ready descriptor.
test       t/024-mask-restored.c

assertion  XSH.poll.025
anchor     functions/poll.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2001
says       nfds greater than {OPEN_MAX} (found with sysconf(_SC_OPEN_MAX))
           makes poll() and ppoll() return -1 with EINVAL.
note       Not applicable (NOTINUSE) when the limit is indeterminate or too
           large for the test to build the array.
test       t/025-einval-nfds.c

assertion  XSH.poll.026
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       O_NONBLOCK does not affect poll() and ppoll(): the read end of an
           empty pipe with O_NONBLOCK set, polled with a 250 ms timeout,
           does not return before the interval has elapsed (allowing for the
           clock's resolution) and gives 0.
test       t/026-nonblock-unaffected.c

assertion  XSH.poll.027
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       An error that read() or write() would report and that comes only
           from the state of the object is POLLERR: the write end of a pipe
           whose read end is closed (a write would give EPIPE), polled for
           POLLOUT, has POLLERR set in revents.
test       t/027-pollerr-epipe.c

assertion  XSH.poll.028
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       POLLERR is reported although it was not requested: the same pipe
           write end with events 0 has POLLERR set in revents and the call
           returns 1.
test       t/028-pollerr-unrequested.c

assertion  XSH.poll.029
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A listening socket is not ready for reading with no connection
           pending, and polls ready (POLLIN) once a connection is available.
test       t/029-listening-socket.c

assertion  XSH.poll.030
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Sockets and FIFOs are supported: a socket pair end gives POLLIN
           after the peer sends a byte, and a FIFO read end opened
           nonblocking gives POLLIN after a writer wrote.
test       t/030-socket-fifo.c

assertion  XSH.poll.031
anchor     functions/poll.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A ppoll() timeout of 31 days is supported: with a ready pipe the
           call returns 1 rather than failing.
note       The page requires a maximum timeout of at least 31 days for
           ppoll() (not for poll()).
test       t/031-timeout-31-days.c
